            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0180" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg46"/>

                <head>No. 43.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Bounder de Melsbroeck to Mr.
                        Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Belgium</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-29"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 29, 1888</date>.
                        (Received March 1.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: The King of the Belgians
                    has offered an annual prize of 25,000 francs, the object of which is to
                    encourage intellectual effort, and I have the honor to transmit to your
                    excellency the inclosed notice, which summarizes the conditions on which the
                    prize for 1893 will be awarded. The award will be made to the best work on the
                    means of procuring, in abundance and at small cost, the best quality of potable
                    water for large cities, especially for Brussels and its suburbs.</p>
                <p>As citizens of the United States are invited to compete for this prize, I take
                    the liberty to beg your excellency to cause this matter to be widely made
                    known.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Th. de Bounder de
                        Melsbroeck.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d43-a1.xml" xpointer="d43-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
